  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Arrhenius equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>Ae</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>Ea</mi><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>logk</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>logA</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8203;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>mx</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>, the equation of straight line</p><p>The value of log <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math> should increase uniformily with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math>&nbsp;or decrease with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mfrac></math>.</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/dc277033-e689-451f-957f-db816643eb9f-image.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 185px;\" /></p><p>From this, that the slope is negative, which means that angle with x - axis is greater than 90&deg; also that the point on which the straight line of graph intercepts the y - axis is log A which is positive.</p><p>Hence all the conclusions point out towards option b as it has negative slope and a positive y intercept.</p>",
